  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0002445 From Weather Data to Actionable Information for a Climate-Smart Horticultural Sector in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0002445 The central goal of the proposed project is to build a portfolio of digital weather and climate related services for the horticultural sector in Ghana. In order to reach the overall goal,  the following activities will be conducted: - The TAHMO network will be enlarged to fill existing gaps, while enlarging the operational up time from 90% to 95% of the time. - A WRF system will be set up for Ghana which is fed by the TAHMO data to  provide farmers with up to date weather forecasts. - Farmers will be consulted in to asses their information needs and the value of the information offered to them. - It will be assed how the information from TAHMO can be most effectively be communicated to the farmers who need and use the data. - The cost will be commercialized through integrators for less than 2 euros per farmer per season. - once the ecosystem of creating and marketing of weather and climate information is set up, it can be extended and diversified to other sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
